    "abstract": "Diffusion models give state-of-the-art synthesis but are costly in pixel space. Latent diffusion models apply diffusion in the latent space of pretrained autoencoders, balancing complexity reduction and detail preservation. Cross-attention layers make them flexible generators for conditions such as text or boxes. LDMs set a new state of the art for inpainting and are competitive on unconditional generation, super-resolution and text-to-image at much lower cost.",
    "domain": "CV",
    "key_claims": [
      "Separating perceptual compression (autoencoder) from semantic generation (diffusion in latent space) greatly reduces compute while keeping quality.",
      "Downsampling factors f = 4 to 16 offer the best trade-off between efficiency and fidelity; f = 1 trains slowly and large f loses detail.",
      "Cross-attention conditioning in the UNet enables text-to-image, layout-to-image and class-conditional synthesis.",
      "LDMs reach FID 5.11 on CelebA-HQ 256, 3.60 on class-conditional ImageNet 256 (with guidance) and 12.63 on MS-COCO text-to-image."
    ],
    "parsed_at": "2026-10-23T12:00:00+05:30",
    "arxivist_version": "1.0"
  },
